('Drosophila', 'dm3', 'chr3L:27,169,029-27,169,030', 'VK00029', 'P[acman] BAC-transgenesis docking site, located in heterochromatin on 3L. Coordinate from the official P[acman] project resource page. Heterochromatic location is a real, independent caveat -- heterochromatin is a classic silencing-prone environment; use with caution unless heterochromatic silencing is specifically desired. This caveat is about chromatin state, not about genome-build certainty.', 'low', 'Heterochromatic location -- plausible silencing risk, not experimentally ruled out here', 'Whole organism / germline (fly transgenesis; not tissue-restricted).', '17008526', 'P[acman]: a BAC transgenic platform for targeted insertion of large DNA fragments in D. melanogaster', true, false),
